id:                     E2180
trigger_tool:           make|cmake|conan
phase:                  compilation|testing
error_signature:        make: jobserver mkfifo: .*Operation not permitted
severity:               2
category:               gnu-make|jobserver|hmdfs|fifo|ohos
match_keywords:         jobserver, mkfifo, GMfifo, Operation not permitted, HMDFS, make, Conan
title:                  Distinguish a nonfatal GNU make jobserver FIFO warning from an actual HMDFS build failure
root_cause:             GNU make may attempt to create a FIFO jobserver endpoint under task-local TMPDIR on HMDFS, where FIFO creation is denied. It can fall back and complete a serial or nested build, so the warning alone does not establish that the build or tests failed.
affected_scope:         HarmonyOS PC builds using GNU make or CMake Unix Makefiles with TMPDIR on HMDFS; especially nested Conan build and test_package invocations.
verification_cmd:       Retain the full build log and command exit code; confirm package archive creation and an installed-package consumer run; compare the mkfifo warning with the actual first fatal error, if any.
rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           bound-target-make-parallelism-and-check-terminal-result
rec_description:        Use -j1 for an upstream target whose HMDFS jobserver behavior prevents reliable parallel work, but do not infer success or failure from the warning's presence. Confirm the exact conan create return code, package artifacts, upstream test denominator, and consumer execution.
rec_command:            autotools.make(args=['-j1']); autotools.make(target='check', args=['-j1']); then verify conan create RC and test_package execution
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               recipe-build-and-evidence
fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      move-jobserver-temporary-area
fallback_description:   Where policy permits a task-private native filesystem, use it for TMPDIR and rerun; never redirect temporary files into another task's root.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          manual
forbid_1_pattern:       grep.*mkfifo.*fail
forbid_1_reason:        A warning can coexist with a zero-exit build and successful consumer; text matching alone misclassifies the terminal result.
forbid_1_consequence:   A valid package can be incorrectly discarded.
forbid_2_pattern:       ignore.*nonzero.*exit
forbid_2_reason:        The warning may also precede an independent fatal compile error; it is not a blanket waiver of command failure.
forbid_2_consequence:   A failed build can be incorrectly reported as passed.
principles:             []
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             [E074, E292]
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []
doc_file:               knowledge/drafts/E2180-draft-2501.md
last_updated:           2026-09-29
source_event:           MAdLib 1.3.0 HarmonyOS PC W3; r3 mkfifo warning plus independent C++ fatal error, final r5 mkfifo warnings in both library and nested Conan CMake consumer phases plus conan create RC0 and consumer 1/1; final log SHA-256 4ca43c65ba0422dbacef04b2f5bc92d864fe7ea0234013ab50efa126a761abe1. E074's fatality inference has a verified counterexample.
metrics_success_count:  1
metrics_fail_count:     1
metrics_confidence:     0.9
metrics_last_used:      2026-09-29
draft:                  true
contributor_id:         2501_91199785
